gn="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Peripheral vascular disease</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">440.xx&#x02013;444.xx; 447.xx; 451.xx&#x02013;453.xx; 557.xx</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cardiac (other)</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">420.xx&#x02013;421.xx; 423.xx&#x02013;424.xx; 429.xx; 785.0&#x02013;785.3</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">V42.2; V43.3</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">491&#x02013;494; 496.xx; 510.xx</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Gastrointestinal bleeding</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">456.0&#x02013;456.2; 530.7; 531&#x02013;534; 569.84; 569.85; 578</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Liver disease</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">570.xx; 571.xx; 572.1; 572.4; 573.1&#x02013;573.3</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">V42.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Dysrhythmia</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">426.xx&#x02013;427.xx</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">V45.0x; V53.3x</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cancer</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">140.xx&#x02013;172.xx; 174.xx&#x02013;208.xx; 230.xx&#x02013;231.xx; 233.xx&#x02013;234.xx</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diabetes</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">250.xx; 357.2; 362.0x; 366.41</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Vascular access</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CPT code 36800 alone; CPT codes 36488, 36489, 36490, 36491, 36533 associated with diagnosis codes 250.xx, 403.xx, 593.xx, V56.x, 996.1, 996.62, 996.73, V45.1, or 580.xx&#x02013;589.xx</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></app></app-group></back><floats-wrap><fig id="f1-tcrm-5-319" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Graphical expression of assumed model. For simplicity and clarity, all baseline variables except persistent anemia appear together in a box labeled &#x0201c;Baseline variables.&#x0201d; An arrow from one box to another, such as &#x0201c;Baseline variables&#x0201d; to &#x0201c;Medical costs,&#x0201d; means that the baseline variables were hypothesized to affect medical costs in the follow-up period. The e<sub>1</sub>&#x02013;e<sub>7</sub> are residuals.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="tcrm-5-319f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-tcrm-5-319" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Flow chart for patient selection from the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid services end-stage renal disease database.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="tcrm-5-319f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-tcrm-5-319" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Patient characteristics: All and by persistent anemia group</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><hr/></th><th align="center" valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1">All<hr/></th><th align="center" valign="bottom" colspan="7" rowspan="1">Baseline months with hemoglobin &#x0003c; 110 g/L<hr/></th><th align="center" valign="bottom" colspan="3" rowspan="1">Baseline mean hemoglobin<hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="bottom" rowspan="